            <div xml:id="d655">

                <pb facs="0942" n="814" sameAs="frus:frus1928v01/pg814"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">820.7961 Dept. of Commerce Flight/22:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Chile</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Collier</hi>)</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-04-16T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 16,
                                1928—4 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>28. Your telegram No. 50, April 11, 2 p.m. The Department prefers that you avoid
                    any discussion of this subject because it does not desire to indicate even
                    indirectly what this Government’s policy might be in case of eventualities to
                    which you allude. This should not prevent you, however, from rendering
                    assistance to the representatives of American companies to obtain a fair
                    consideration of their propositions.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
